  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "A square and an equilateral triangle each have a perimeter of $36$. Find the ratio of the area of the square to the area of the triangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$9:4\\sqrt{3}$.\n\nFind the triangle's altitude using Pythagoras, then compare the two areas.",
      "worked": "The square has side length $36\\div4=9$, and the equilateral triangle has side length $36\\div3=12$.\n\nThe triangle's altitude bisects its base. Let the altitude be $h$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2&=12^2-6^2\\\\h^2&=108\\\\h&=6\\sqrt{3}\\\\A_{\\text{square}}&=9^2\\\\A_{\\text{square}}&=81\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\frac{12\\times6\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=36\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore the ratio is $81:36\\sqrt{3}=9:4\\sqrt{3}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 92
  },
